{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwM5inEeYCBWnVFawkui","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. It has run once and its status is \"ok\".\n\n**What the data holds:** The Kibana Sample Data Logs view is web server traffic. Its main fields are `timestamp`, `response` (the HTTP status, stored as a string), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url`, `request` and `agent`.\n\n**Dashboard \"EFF-f2528d7d Web logs overview\"** (`eff-f2528d7d-web-logs-overview-921001af86a2`) has four panels:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Responses by status code\n- Average bytes by file extension\n\n**Rule \"EFF-f2528d7d 5xx spike\"** (`26a2a9bb-469a-46d7-95db-b4b360d5bf41`):\n- **Type:** an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- **Schedule:** it runs every minute.\n- **Condition:** it fires when more than 10 documents match `response.keyword` against `5[0-9][0-9]` within the last 5 minutes.\n- **Actions:** none, since you didn't ask for any.\n\nI haven't opened the dashboard in Kibana to check that the panels render. The sample data's timestamps may also be old, so the rule may not fire until fresh 5xx documents arrive."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":268,"cache_read_input_tokens":20306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":268},"output_tokens":480,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"46dff3a5-e0e7-4fda-ab37-245e42c87e9f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:50:53.768Z","request_id":"req_011CfwM5iZqMnpvS7a7zPWfc"}
